resolved_issues.body:
@zi-v @arnonsha 
During full chip simulation a bug was found on the clocks bypass logic.

The bug involve the incorrect step down  (div4-to-div2) of the IO clock in the lc_ctrl/clkmgr 
module/s during other clocks bypass modes.

In order to fix the issue, the AST added a new signal to indicate to the lc_ctrl/clkmgr
modules that the IO clock is 48Mhz. 
The interface to the lc_ctrl/clkmgr needs to include a new signal:

-	clk_src_io_48m_o    //  0: 96MHz, 1: 48MHz

This signal is needed to be used for the div4/div2 selection in the lc_ctrl/clkmgr module/s.

The reason that this signal is needed relate to the fact the lc_ctrl/clkmgr moduless are not aware of  clocks  bypass other modes. 

// IO Clock Source is 48MHz
////////////////////////////////////////
// Oscillator source is always 96MHz. 
// External Bypass source is assume to be 96MHz until it is ebabled as 48MHz 
assign clk_src_io_48m_o = io_clk_byp_sel && io_clk_byp_en && !ext_freq_is_96m;

See monorail Issue 101: [Gold] IO clock is 48MHz indication from AST for mode details.

